CMD: for k in ...; do echo $(( $(stat -c%s work) - $(stat -c%s master) )); done
OUT: income 21   expenses 21   savings 21   savings-rate 21
CMD: diff -u <master> <branch> | cat -A
OUT (identical shape in all four files, one hunk, one added line):
     @@ -58,6 +58,7 @@$
                          $
                          $
                          $
     +                    $                       <- 20 spaces + LF, 21 bytes
                          <tr class="hover:bg-gray-50 ..." onclick="openKPIMonthDetail('expenses', '2025-01')">$
Master-native baseline pinned (per the oracle-calibration rule): master already
emits FOUR whitespace-only lines between <tbody> and the first <tr>; the branch
emits FIVE. The regression is exactly one line, not the whole block.

CAUSE — the one template action attempt 3 did NOT trim
(web/templates/components/kpi-detail.html:93):
    {{$noCoverage := and (eq .Type "healthcare") .HealthcareNoCoverageInRange}}
It sits on its own line with NO `{{-`/`-}}` markers, so its surrounding
newline+indent text node is emitted for EVERY kind. The manifest's item 4 added
trims to the two `{{if}}/{{else}}/{{end}}` wrappers only:
  :49 `{{if and (eq .Type "healthcare") .HealthcareNoCoverageInRange -}}`
  :52 `{{- else -}}`  :54 `{{- end}}`
  :114 `{{if $noCoverage -}}` :116 `{{- else -}}` :118 `{{- end}}`
Those two are correct — they account for the drop from +213/+63/+63/+21 to a
uniform +21. Line 93 is the sole remaining source. This is a near-miss: the
missing piece is trim markers on kpi-detail.html:93.

WHAT IS IN SCOPE: ruling KD-2026-08-30d names this explicitly as part of the
attempt-3 contract ("template {{- -}} trim markers so pre-existing kinds' rendered
HTML is byte-identical to master (K5, attempt-2 regression was inert whitespace)"),
and K5 / Design 7 say "byte-identical". No command I can run shows the criterion
met, so I report it not met.

