OBSERVATIONS (backlog, NOT failures)
=====================================================================
O1. The LIVING month-drill negation (handlers.go:755) is guarded only by the
    tier-3 oracle (TestOracleKD1_MonthDrillMatchesSignedRow), which is NOT
    committed into the package — mutation C reverts that one line to Abs and the
    whole repo suite stays GREEN. The healthcare twin IS covered by a committed
    test (TestHandleKPIMonthDetail_HealthcareSignedNotAbs). Promoting the oracle's
    living month-drill check into handlers_http_test.go (V3 pattern) would close it.
O2. handlers_http_test.go:2508 still uses `math.Abs(got-150) > 0.01` for the K3b
    Total-tile figure. Outside K9's wording (which names the two Per-Month tests),
    but it is the same rendered-string-arithmetic class K9 exists to close.
O3. verdictDollarRe (`\$([\d,]+\.\d{2})`) does not capture a leading "-", so
    extractDollarStringAfter returns "$500.00" for a rendered "-$500.00". The
    reconcile test's Total assertion therefore cannot detect a sign flip in the
    Total TILE alone; it detects the mutation only via the row strings and the
    magnitude. Not a defect today (mutation A kills the test), but the helper is
    sign-blind.
O4. formatMoneyExpected remains a hand-maintained mirror of the unexported
    templates.formatMoney (the "dual formatters" class) — carried over from
    KD1.2.checker-tests O1, still open.
O5. handleKPIExport still has no `default` arm (pre-existing on master).
O6. kpis.html:141 (Budget card) still opens the generic expenses modal — the
    spec's own declared backlog item, correctly not touched.
